ner might just say to the NFL find me  I don't care my players want to do it  and that's I stand behind them that  that's all still possible in the NFL  yeah it's absolutely possible it's left  up to the teams now to decide whether or  not they will find players if they  demonstrate but if the league finds a  team though Jim isn't that technically  finding the players by saying that they  that they're not they're not they're not  taking money out of the players pocket  but what we are saying is that is that  is that they still disagree with it and  that might create an issue between the  players and the league despite what you  the intent is to have the relationship  grow is know in a literal sense what  you're saying is absolutely right the  league is not taking money out of the  players pocket which is as you know very  important to a player sure but it is  taking it out of the team's pocket if it  chooses to find them that's the other  thing it says they can find a team will  they find a team we won't know until we  get to that situation so there's still  you know there's a lot of gray here but  the owners felt that they had to do  something and as I understand it when  they broke yesterday there were a group  of roughly nine to ten owners who felt  that they wanted to keep the status quo  in part because they felt that they had  gone through the roughest part of this  that they're doing work with their  players in terms of the social justice  initiative and the things that they are  doing off the field as well to confront  these issues that are important to the  players and so they felt why do we want  to now reignite this when we're only  talking about a handful of players who  were actually demonstrating but the  other thing is there was another group  of owners as I was told a handful or so  who were more adamant that they wanted a  strong policy in place and they wanted  the teams to have control over that and  then the rest of the owners I was told  wanted 